IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `chr-dates`

-- Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006 (Victoria) -- the rules, as the PERSON meets them.
--
-- SEAT: a person injured in State custody or care, or by a public body, who has a cause of action of their own apart
-- from the Charter (in negligence, for false imprisonment or battery, under a statute, or for judicial review). The
-- Charter is the least direct of the claims laws: it gives no claim and no damages of its own (s 39), but it can add a
-- ground of unlawfulness to the claim the person already has (s 38, s 39(1)), and it changes how the court reads any
-- Victorian statute in the case (s 32). The public authority, the court, the Attorney-General and the Commission get no
-- seat.
--
-- In this module: s 3 (child, statutory provision, act), s 4 (public authority), s 6(1) (only persons have rights),
-- Part 2 (each right in the focus limb by limb: ss 9, 10, 13, 21, 22, 23, 24; the other rights named), s 7(2) (limits),
-- s 31(6), (7) (override declarations), s 32 (interpretation), s 35 (notice to the Attorney-General and the Commission,
-- a duty on the person as a party: the one regulative rule), s 36(5) (what a declaration of inconsistent interpretation
-- does not do), s 38 (conduct of public authorities), s 39 (legal proceedings), s 49(2), (3) (transitional). The
-- exported questions are in chr-seat.l4; the worked cases in chr-cases.l4.
--
-- Judgments the Charter leaves to a court (whether treatment was cruel, inhuman or degrading; whether an interference was
-- arbitrary; whether a function is of a public nature; whether a limit is demonstrably justified; whether consideration
-- was proper) are inputs, answered conditionally, never decided here.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Charter of
-- Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006, Act No. 43/2006, Version No. 015 (1 June 2022), not the authorised
-- version. (c) State of Victoria; published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No
-- part may be reproduced except in accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of
-- 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006: the rules`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 3 -- definitions; s 6(1) -- who has human rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 3 "child means a person under 18 years of age". A "means" definition.
GIVEN `the age in whole years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a child` `the age in whole years` IF
    `the age in whole years` LESS THAN 18

-- s 3 "person means a human being"; s 6(1) "Only persons have human rights. All persons have the human rights set out
-- in Part 2." (Note: "Corporations do not have human rights.") "Only": a closed list, so a body that is not a human
-- being has none (JUST FALSE kind).
GIVEN `a human being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6(1) -- has the human rights in Part 2` `a human being` IF
    `a human being`

-- s 3 "statutory provision means an Act (including this Charter) or a subordinate instrument or a provision of an Act
-- ... or of a subordinate instrument". "Act" and "subordinate instrument" are borrowed (Interpretation of Legislation
-- Act 1984, not deposited): read as a Victorian Act and an instrument made under one (fork F6).
DECLARE `Kind of law` IS ONE OF
    `a Victorian Act`
    `a Victorian subordinate instrument (regulations, rules or orders made under a Victorian Act)`
    `a Commonwealth Act, or an instrument made under one`
    `the common law (judge-made law, such as the law of negligence)`
    `the law of another State, a Territory or another country`

GIVEN `the law` IS A `Kind of law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- a statutory provision` `the law` IF
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `a Victorian Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Victorian subordinate instrument (regulations, rules or orders made under a Victorian Act)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 4 -- what a public authority is`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- The kinds of body s 4(1) names, in its order, with the bodies it excludes. "Public official within the meaning of the
-- Public Administration Act 2004" and "Council ... within the meaning of the Local Government Act 2020" are borrowed:
-- the person picks the kind (fork F1).
DECLARE `Kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `a public official, such as a public servant, a department head or the staff of a public entity (Public Administration Act 2004)`
    `a body set up by an Act or another statutory provision (for example a statutory authority, a public hospital or a school council)`
    `Victoria Police (a police officer or other member of Victoria Police)`
    `a council, a councillor or a member of council staff (Local Government Act 2020)`
    `a Minister`
    `members of a Parliamentary Committee`
    `Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament`
    `a court or a tribunal`
    `another body or person not set up by statute (for example a private company running a prison, a care provider or a contractor)`

DECLARE `Public authority` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a public official (s 4(1)(a))`
    `yes: an entity established by a statutory provision that has functions of a public nature (s 4(1)(b))`
    `yes: an entity exercising functions of a public nature on behalf of the State or a public authority (s 4(1)(c))`
    `yes: Victoria Police (s 4(1)(d))`
    `yes: a Council, a Councillor or a member of Council staff (s 4(1)(e))`
    `yes: a Minister (s 4(1)(f))`
    `yes: members of a Parliamentary Committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(g))`
    `yes: an entity declared by the regulations to be a public authority (s 4(1)(h))`
    `yes: a court or tribunal acting in an administrative capacity (not excluded by s 4(1)(j); a public authority under s 4(1)(b) when established by a statutory provision)`
    `no: Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament, is not a public authority (s 4(1)(i))`
    `no: a court or tribunal is not a public authority except when it is acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(j))`
    `no: an entity declared by the regulations not to be a public authority (s 4(1)(k))`
    `no: none of the kinds of public authority in s 4(1) (a)-(h)`

-- s 4(1) "a public authority is-- (a) ... (h) ... but does not include-- (i) ... (j) ... (k) ...". Read as a "means"
-- definition: a body in none of (a)-(h) is not a public authority (JUST FALSE kind; fork F2). The exclusions are flat
-- negatives and come first. "Functions of a public nature" (s 4(2), (3): factors, not exhaustive, not conclusive),
-- "on behalf of the State or a public authority" (s 4(4), (5)) and "acting in an administrative capacity" are
-- judgments: asked. The regulations under s 46(2)(a)-(c) are not deposited: whether a body is declared is asked.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of body`
      `has functions of a public nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exercising them on behalf of the State or a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acting in an administrative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `declared by the regulations to be one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `declared by the regulations not to be one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Public authority`
`s 4 -- public authority` `the kind` `has functions of a public nature` `exercising them on behalf of the State or a public authority` `acting in an administrative capacity` `declared by the regulations to be one` `declared by the regulations not to be one` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament`
        THEN `no: Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament, is not a public authority (s 4(1)(i))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a court or a tribunal`) AND (NOT `acting in an administrative capacity`)
        THEN `no: a court or tribunal is not a public authority except when it is acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(j))`
        IF `declared by the regulations not to be one`
        THEN `no: an entity declared by the regulations not to be a public authority (s 4(1)(k))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a public official, such as a public servant, a department head or the staff of a public entity (Public Administration Act 2004)`
        THEN `yes: a public official (s 4(1)(a))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `a body set up by an Act or another statutory provision (for example a statutory authority, a public hospital or a school council)`) AND `has functions of a public nature`
        THEN `yes: an entity established by a statutory provision that has functions of a public nature (s 4(1)(b))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `another body or person not set up by statute (for example a private company running a prison, a care provider or a contractor)`) AND `has functions of a public nature` AND `exercising them on behalf of the State or a public authority`
        THEN `yes: an entity exercising functions of a public nature on behalf of the State or a public authority (s 4(1)(c))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `Victoria Police (a police officer or other member of Victoria Police)`
        THEN `yes: Victoria Police (s 4(1)(d))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a council, a councillor or a member of council staff (Local Government Act 2020)`
        THEN `yes: a Council, a Councillor or a member of Council staff (s 4(1)(e))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a Minister`
        THEN `yes: a Minister (s 4(1)(f))`
        IF (`the kind` EQUALS `members of a Parliamentary Committee`) AND `acting in an administrative capacity`
        THEN `yes: members of a Parliamentary Committee acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(g))`
        IF `declared by the regulations to be one`
        THEN `yes: an entity declared by the regulations to be a public authority (s 4(1)(h))`
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `a court or a tribunal`
        THEN `yes: a court or tribunal acting in an administrative capacity (not excluded by s 4(1)(j); a public authority under s 4(1)(b) when established by a statutory provision)`
        OTHERWISE `no: none of the kinds of public authority in s 4(1) (a)-(h)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Public authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a public authority` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `no: Parliament, or a person exercising functions in connection with proceedings in Parliament, is not a public authority (s 4(1)(i))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no: a court or tribunal is not a public authority except when it is acting in an administrative capacity (s 4(1)(j))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no: an entity declared by the regulations not to be a public authority (s 4(1)(k))` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no: none of the kinds of public authority in s 4(1) (a)-(h)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `Part 2 -- the human rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- Every right in Part 2, by section (ss 8-27). The focus rights (ss 9, 10, 13, 21, 22, 23, 24) are encoded limb by
-- limb below; the others are named here so that the s 38 question can be asked of any of them, with whether the act
-- limited the right asked as the court's finding.
DECLARE `Charter right` IS ONE OF
    `s 8 recognition and equality before the law`
    `s 9 the right to life`
    `s 10 protection from torture and cruel, inhuman or degrading treatment`
    `s 11 freedom from forced work`
    `s 12 freedom of movement`
    `s 13 privacy and reputation`
    `s 14 freedom of thought, conscience, religion and belief`
    `s 15 freedom of expression`
    `s 16 peaceful assembly and freedom of association`
    `s 17 protection of families and children`
    `s 18 taking part in public life`
    `s 19 cultural rights`
    `s 20 property rights`
    `s 21 liberty and security of person`
    `s 22 humane treatment when deprived of liberty`
    `s 23 children in the criminal process`
    `s 24 fair hearing`
    `s 25 rights in criminal proceedings`
    `s 26 the right not to be tried or punished more than once`
    `s 27 protection from retrospective criminal laws`

-- The limbs of the focus rights, each a thing the text says a person has a right to, or must not be subjected to.
DECLARE `Charter limb` IS ONE OF
    `s 9: the right to life`
    `s 9: arbitrarily deprived of life`
    `s 10(a): subjected to torture`
    `s 10(b): treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way`
    `s 10(c): subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without full, free and informed consent`
    `s 13(a): privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with`
    `s 13(b): reputation unlawfully attacked`
    `s 21(1): the right to liberty and security`
    `s 21(2): arbitrary arrest or detention`
    `s 21(3): deprived of liberty other than on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established by law`
    `s 21(4): not informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason for it`
    `s 21(4): not promptly informed about proceedings to be brought`
    `s 21(5)(a): not promptly brought before a court on a criminal charge`
    `s 21(5)(b): not brought to trial without unreasonable delay`
    `s 21(5)(c): not released when paragraph (a) or (b) was not complied with`
    `s 21(6): automatically detained in custody while awaiting trial`
    `s 21(7): the court did not decide on the lawfulness of the detention without delay`
    `s 21(7): the court did not order release after finding the detention unlawful`
    `s 21(8): imprisoned only because of an inability to perform a contractual obligation`
    `s 22(1): not treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person`
    `s 22(2): an unconvicted detainee not segregated from convicted persons, where that was not reasonably necessary`
    `s 22(3): an unconvicted detainee not treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted`
    `s 23(1): a detained child not segregated from all detained adults`
    `s 23(2): an accused child not brought to trial as quickly as possible`
    `s 23(3): a convicted child not treated in a way appropriate for the child's age`
    `s 24(1): the proceeding not decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing`
    `s 24(3): the judgment or decision not made public`

-- A limb in the list if the facts meet it.
GIVEN `it is met` IS A BOOLEAN, `the limb` IS A `Charter limb`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`when` `it is met` `the limb` MEANS
    IF `it is met` THEN LIST `the limb` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 9 "Every person has the right to life and has the right not to be arbitrarily deprived of life." The first limb is
-- not spelt out: whether an act or failure (for example a failure to protect a person in custody) limits it is the
-- court's reading, asked. The second limb needs a death and is for those who claim for it (fork F3).
GIVEN `the court holds the act limited my right to life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a life was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `arbitrarily` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 9 -- limbs limited` `the court holds the act limited my right to life` `a life was taken` `arbitrarily` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `the court holds the act limited my right to life` `s 9: the right to life`),
        (`when` (`a life was taken` AND `arbitrarily`) `s 9: arbitrarily deprived of life`))

-- s 10 "A person must not be-- (a) subjected to torture; or (b) treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading
-- way; or (c) subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without that person's full, free and
-- informed consent." (a) and (b) are the court's characterisation (asked); (c) turns on facts.
GIVEN `torture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cruel, inhuman or degrading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `full, free and informed consent given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 10 -- limbs limited` `torture` `cruel, inhuman or degrading` `subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` `full, free and informed consent given` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `torture` `s 10(a): subjected to torture`),
        (`when` `cruel, inhuman or degrading` `s 10(b): treated or punished in a cruel, inhuman or degrading way`),
        (`when` (`subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment` AND (NOT `full, free and informed consent given`)) `s 10(c): subjected to medical or scientific experimentation or treatment without full, free and informed consent`))

-- s 13 "A person has the right-- (a) not to have that person's privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or
-- arbitrarily interfered with; and (b) not to have that person's reputation unlawfully attacked." "Unlawfully" and
-- "arbitrarily" are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interference was arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reputation attacked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attack was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 13 -- limbs limited` `privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` `the interference was unlawful` `the interference was arbitrary` `reputation attacked` `the attack was unlawful` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`privacy, family, home or correspondence interfered with` AND (`the interference was unlawful` OR `the interference was arbitrary`)) `s 13(a): privacy, family, home or correspondence unlawfully or arbitrarily interfered with`),
        (`when` (`reputation attacked` AND `the attack was unlawful`) `s 13(b): reputation unlawfully attacked`))

-- s 21(1)-(4), (7), (8): arrest and detention, whatever the reason for it.
-- (1) "Every person has the right to liberty and security." General: the court's reading, asked.
-- (2) "must not be subjected to arbitrary arrest or detention." Arbitrary: asked.
-- (3) "must not be deprived of that person's liberty except on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established
--     by law." "Except": the deprivation is a limit unless both hold.
-- (4) "must be informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason ... and must be promptly informed about any
--     proceedings to be brought". "At the time" and "promptly": the court's (asked as whether it was done).
-- (7) "the court must-- (a) make a decision without delay; and (b) order the release of the person if it finds that the
--     detention is unlawful." Only where the person applied (the right to apply is the person's; fork F4).
-- (8) "must not be imprisoned only because of that person's inability to perform a contractual obligation."
GIVEN `the court holds the act limited my liberty or security of person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was arrested or detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was arbitrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on grounds established by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in accordance with procedures established by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `told the reason at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings were to be brought against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `promptly told about them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I applied to a court about the lawfulness of my detention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court decided without delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court found the detention unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court ordered my release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `imprisoned only because I could not perform a contractual obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 21 -- arrest and detention limbs limited` `the court holds the act limited my liberty or security of person` `I was arrested or detained` `it was arbitrary` `on grounds established by law` `in accordance with procedures established by law` `told the reason at the time` `proceedings were to be brought against me` `promptly told about them` `I applied to a court about the lawfulness of my detention` `the court decided without delay` `the court found the detention unlawful` `the court ordered my release` `imprisoned only because I could not perform a contractual obligation` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` `the court holds the act limited my liberty or security of person` `s 21(1): the right to liberty and security`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND `it was arbitrary`) `s 21(2): arbitrary arrest or detention`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND (NOT (`on grounds established by law` AND `in accordance with procedures established by law`))) `s 21(3): deprived of liberty other than on grounds, and in accordance with procedures, established by law`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND (NOT `told the reason at the time`)) `s 21(4): not informed at the time of arrest or detention of the reason for it`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND `proceedings were to be brought against me` AND (NOT `promptly told about them`)) `s 21(4): not promptly informed about proceedings to be brought`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND `I applied to a court about the lawfulness of my detention` AND (NOT `the court decided without delay`)) `s 21(7): the court did not decide on the lawfulness of the detention without delay`),
        (`when` (`I was arrested or detained` AND `I applied to a court about the lawfulness of my detention` AND `the court found the detention unlawful` AND (NOT `the court ordered my release`)) `s 21(7): the court did not order release after finding the detention unlawful`),
        (`when` `imprisoned only because I could not perform a contractual obligation` `s 21(8): imprisoned only because of an inability to perform a contractual obligation`))

-- s 21(5), (6): a person arrested or detained on a criminal charge, and a person awaiting trial.
-- (5) "(a) must be promptly brought before a court; and (b) has the right to be brought to trial without unreasonable
--     delay; and (c) must be released if paragraph (a) or (b) is not complied with."
-- (6) "must not be automatically detained in custody, but that person's release may be subject to guarantees to attend".
-- "Promptly", "unreasonable delay" and "automatically" are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `held on a criminal charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `promptly brought before a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought to trial without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `released` IS A BOOLEAN
      `awaiting trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `automatically detained in custody` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 21 -- criminal charge limbs limited` `held on a criminal charge` `promptly brought before a court` `brought to trial without unreasonable delay` `released` `awaiting trial` `automatically detained in custody` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`held on a criminal charge` AND (NOT `promptly brought before a court`)) `s 21(5)(a): not promptly brought before a court on a criminal charge`),
        (`when` (`held on a criminal charge` AND (NOT `brought to trial without unreasonable delay`)) `s 21(5)(b): not brought to trial without unreasonable delay`),
        (`when` (`held on a criminal charge` AND ((NOT `promptly brought before a court`) OR (NOT `brought to trial without unreasonable delay`)) AND (NOT `released`)) `s 21(5)(c): not released when paragraph (a) or (b) was not complied with`),
        (`when` (`awaiting trial` AND `automatically detained in custody`) `s 21(6): automatically detained in custody while awaiting trial`))

-- The person's position in the criminal process, for ss 22 and 23.
DECLARE `My position` IS ONE OF
    `accused of an offence and detained`
    `accused of an offence and not detained`
    `detained without charge (for example by police, or under mental health or other law)`
    `convicted of an offence`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `the position` IS A `My position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge` `the position` IF
    CONSIDER `the position`
    WHEN `accused of an offence and detained` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `detained without charge (for example by police, or under mental health or other law)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 22 "(1) All persons deprived of liberty must be treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of
-- the human person. (2) An accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge must be segregated from
-- persons who have been convicted of offences, except where reasonably necessary. (3) An accused person who is detained
-- or a person detained without charge must be treated in a way that is appropriate for a person who has not been
-- convicted." "Deprived of liberty" reaches care as well as custody (asked). "Except where reasonably necessary" is the
-- court's (asked).
GIVEN `deprived of liberty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated with humanity and respect for dignity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the position` IS A `My position`
      `held with convicted persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as appropriate for a person not convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 22 -- limbs limited` `deprived of liberty` `treated with humanity and respect for dignity` `the position` `held with convicted persons` `that was reasonably necessary` `treated as appropriate for a person not convicted` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        (`when` (`deprived of liberty` AND (NOT `treated with humanity and respect for dignity`)) `s 22(1): not treated with humanity and with respect for the inherent dignity of the human person`),
        (`when` (`an accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge` `the position` AND `held with convicted persons` AND (NOT `that was reasonably necessary`)) `s 22(2): an unconvicted detainee not segregated from convicted persons, where that was not reasonably necessary`),
        (`when` (`an accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge` `the position` AND (NOT `treated as appropriate for a person not convicted`)) `s 22(3): an unconvicted detainee not treated in a way appropriate for a person who has not been convicted`))

-- s 23 "(1) An accused child who is detained or a child detained without charge must be segregated from all detained
-- adults. (2) An accused child must be brought to trial as quickly as possible. (3) A child who has been convicted of an
-- offence must be treated in a way that is appropriate for that child's age." Child: s 3 (under 18), at the time.
-- No exception in (1) (contrast s 22(2)). "As quickly as possible" and "appropriate" are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `my age at the time` IS A NUMBER
      `the position` IS A `My position`
      `held with detained adults` IS A BOOLEAN
      `brought to trial as quickly as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as appropriate for my age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 23 -- limbs limited` `my age at the time` `the position` `held with detained adults` `brought to trial as quickly as possible` `treated as appropriate for my age` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 3 -- a child` `my age at the time`)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE concat (LIST
        (`when` (`an accused person who is detained or a person detained without charge` `the position` AND `held with detained adults`) `s 23(1): a detained child not segregated from all detained adults`),
        (`when` (((`the position` EQUALS `accused of an offence and detained`) OR (`the position` EQUALS `accused of an offence and not detained`)) AND (NOT `brought to trial as quickly as possible`)) `s 23(2): an accused child not brought to trial as quickly as possible`),
        (`when` ((`the position` EQUALS `convicted of an offence`) AND (NOT `treated as appropriate for my age`)) `s 23(3): a convicted child not treated in a way appropriate for the child's age`))

-- s 24 "(1) A person charged with a criminal offence or a party to a civil proceeding has the right to have the charge
-- or proceeding decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing.
-- (2) Despite subsection (1), a court or tribunal may exclude ... the general public from all or part of a hearing if
-- permitted to do so by a law other than this Charter. (3) All judgments or decisions made by a court or tribunal in a
-- criminal or civil proceeding must be made public unless the best interests of a child otherwise requires or a law
-- other than this Charter otherwise permits." Competent, independent, impartial and fair are the court's (asked).
GIVEN `a party to a civil proceeding, or charged with an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `competent, independent and impartial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing was fair` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing was public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another law permitted excluding the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment or decision was made public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a child's best interests or another law permitted not making it public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Charter limb`
`s 24 -- limbs limited` `a party to a civil proceeding, or charged with an offence` `competent, independent and impartial` `the hearing was fair` `the hearing was public` `another law permitted excluding the public` `the judgment or decision was made public` `a child's best interests or another law permitted not making it public` MEANS
    IF NOT `a party to a civil proceeding, or charged with an offence`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE concat (LIST
        (`when` ((NOT `competent, independent and impartial`) OR (NOT `the hearing was fair`) OR ((NOT `the hearing was public`) AND (NOT `another law permitted excluding the public`))) `s 24(1): the proceeding not decided by a competent, independent and impartial court or tribunal after a fair and public hearing`),
        (`when` ((NOT `the judgment or decision was made public`) AND (NOT `a child's best interests or another law permitted not making it public`)) `s 24(3): the judgment or decision not made public`))

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 7(2) -- when a right may be limited`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 7(2) "A human right may be subject under law only to such reasonable limits as can be demonstrably justified in a
-- free and democratic society ...". "Only": a limit that is not under law, or not demonstrably justified, is not one
-- the Charter allows (JUST FALSE kind). Whether a limit is justified, weighing (a)-(e), is the court's (asked).
GIVEN `a right was limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 7(2), 38(1) -- incompatible with a human right` `a right was limited` `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified` IF
    `a right was limited` AND (NOT `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified`)

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 38 -- conduct of public authorities`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 38(1) "Subject to this section, it is unlawful for a public authority to act in a way that is incompatible with a
-- human right or, in making a decision, to fail to give proper consideration to a relevant human right."
-- s 3 "act includes a failure to act and a proposal to act".
-- s 38(2) "Subsection (1) does not apply if, as a result of a statutory provision or a provision made by or under an Act
-- of the Commonwealth or otherwise under law, the public authority could not reasonably have acted differently or made
-- a different decision."
-- s 38(3) "This section does not apply to an act or decision of a private nature."
-- s 38(4) "Subsection (1) does not require a public authority to act in a way, or make a decision, that has the effect of
-- impeding or preventing a religious body ... from acting in conformity with the religious doctrines, beliefs or
-- principles in accordance with which the religious body operates."
-- s 49(3) "Division 4 of Part 3 does not apply to any act or decision made by a public authority before the
-- commencement of that Division" (1 January 2008).
DECLARE `Unlawful under s 38` IS ONE OF
    `yes: unlawful, both as an act incompatible with a human right and as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
    `yes: unlawful as an act incompatible with a human right (s 38(1))`
    `yes: unlawful as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
    `no: s 38 binds only public authorities, and this body is not one (s 4)`
    `no: Division 4 of Part 3 does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
    `no: s 38 does not apply to an act or decision of a private nature (s 38(3))`
    `no: s 38(1) does not apply, as the public authority could not reasonably have acted differently or made a different decision because of a statutory provision or other law (s 38(2))`
    `no: s 38(1) does not require the public authority to act in a way that impedes a religious body acting in conformity with its doctrines, beliefs or principles (s 38(4))`
    `no: on these facts the act was not incompatible with a human right, and any decision was made with proper consideration of the relevant human rights (s 38(1) not met)`

GIVEN `a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the act or decision` IS A DATE
      `of a private nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acting compatibly would have impeded a religious body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a right was limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it made a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it gave proper consideration to the relevant human rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Unlawful under s 38`
`s 38 -- unlawful` `a public authority` `the day of the act or decision` `of a private nature` `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law` `acting compatibly would have impeded a religious body` `a right was limited` `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified` `it made a decision` `it gave proper consideration to the relevant human rights` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a public authority`
        THEN `no: s 38 binds only public authorities, and this body is not one (s 4)`
        IF `the day` `the day of the act or decision` `is before` `the day Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 came into operation`
        THEN `no: Division 4 of Part 3 does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
        IF `of a private nature`
        THEN `no: s 38 does not apply to an act or decision of a private nature (s 38(3))`
        IF `could not reasonably have acted differently because of law`
        THEN `no: s 38(1) does not apply, as the public authority could not reasonably have acted differently or made a different decision because of a statutory provision or other law (s 38(2))`
        IF `acting compatibly would have impeded a religious body`
        THEN `no: s 38(1) does not require the public authority to act in a way that impedes a religious body acting in conformity with its doctrines, beliefs or principles (s 38(4))`
        IF `incompatible` AND `no proper consideration`
        THEN `yes: unlawful, both as an act incompatible with a human right and as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
        IF `incompatible`
        THEN `yes: unlawful as an act incompatible with a human right (s 38(1))`
        IF `no proper consideration`
        THEN `yes: unlawful as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))`
        OTHERWISE `no: on these facts the act was not incompatible with a human right, and any decision was made with proper consideration of the relevant human rights (s 38(1) not met)`
    WHERE
        `incompatible` MEANS `ss 7(2), 38(1) -- incompatible with a human right` `a right was limited` `the limit is under law and demonstrably justified`
        `no proper consideration` MEANS `it made a decision` AND (NOT `it gave proper consideration to the relevant human rights`)

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Unlawful under s 38`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is unlawful under s 38` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `yes: unlawful, both as an act incompatible with a human right and as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `yes: unlawful as an act incompatible with a human right (s 38(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `yes: unlawful as a decision made without proper consideration of a relevant human right (s 38(1))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 39 -- legal proceedings: a Charter ground rides on another claim; no damages of its own`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 39(1) "If, otherwise than because of this Charter, a person may seek any relief or remedy in respect of an act or
-- decision of a public authority on the ground that the act or decision was unlawful, that person may seek that relief
-- or remedy on a ground of unlawfulness arising because of this Charter."
-- "If": without a claim that exists apart from the Charter, s 39(1) gives the person nothing (JUST FALSE kind). Whether
-- the person has such a claim (judicial review, a tort claim, a statutory claim) is that other law's (asked; fork F7).
DECLARE `A Charter ground` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may seek the same relief or remedy on a ground of unlawfulness arising because of the Charter (s 39(1)), alongside my other claim`
    `no: the Charter gives no claim of its own; s 39(1) lets me add a Charter ground only to a claim I have apart from the Charter`
    `no: s 39 is in Division 4 of Part 3, which does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
    `no: s 39(1) is about acts and decisions of a public authority, and this body is not one (s 4)`

GIVEN `a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the act or decision` IS A DATE
      `I have a claim apart from the Charter on the ground the act was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A Charter ground`
`s 39(1) -- a Charter ground` `a public authority` `the day of the act or decision` `I have a claim apart from the Charter on the ground the act was unlawful` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a public authority`
        THEN `no: s 39(1) is about acts and decisions of a public authority, and this body is not one (s 4)`
        IF `the day` `the day of the act or decision` `is before` `the day Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 came into operation`
        THEN `no: s 39 is in Division 4 of Part 3, which does not apply to an act or decision made before 1 January 2008 (s 49(3))`
        IF `I have a claim apart from the Charter on the ground the act was unlawful`
        THEN `yes: I may seek the same relief or remedy on a ground of unlawfulness arising because of the Charter (s 39(1)), alongside my other claim`
        OTHERWISE `no: the Charter gives no claim of its own; s 39(1) lets me add a Charter ground only to a claim I have apart from the Charter`

-- s 39(3) "A person is not entitled to be awarded any damages because of a breach of this Charter."
-- s 39(4) "Nothing in this section affects any right a person may have to damages apart from the operation of this
-- section." A flat negative (JUST FALSE kind, always), with the other right to damages kept.
DECLARE `Damages for a Charter breach` IS ONE OF
    `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); my right to damages under my other claim is not affected (s 39(4))`
    `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); and on my facts I have no other right to damages for the act`

GIVEN `I have a right to damages apart from the Charter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Damages for a Charter breach`
`s 39(3), (4) -- damages` `I have a right to damages apart from the Charter` MEANS
    IF `I have a right to damages apart from the Charter`
    THEN `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); my right to damages under my other claim is not affected (s 39(4))`
    ELSE `no damages because of a breach of the Charter (s 39(3)); and on my facts I have no other right to damages for the act`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 31, 32, 36(5), 49 -- reading the statutes in my case compatibly with my rights`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 31(6) "If an override declaration is made in respect of a statutory provision, then to the extent of the
-- declaration this Charter has no application to that provision." s 31(7) "A provision of an Act containing an override
-- declaration expires on the 5th anniversary of the day on which that provision comes into operation or on such earlier
-- date as may be specified in that Act." s 31(8): re-enactment restarts it (the person gives the latest). s 31(2): an
-- override for an Act extends to instruments made under it.
-- On and after the expiry day the declaration has expired (fork F9).
GIVEN `an override declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it came into operation` IS A DATE
      `an earlier expiry date is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier expiry date` IS A DATE
      `the day the court reads the provision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(6), (7) -- an override declaration is in force` `an override declaration was made` `the day it came into operation` `an earlier expiry date is specified` `the earlier expiry date` `the day the court reads the provision` IF
        `an override declaration was made`
    AND (NOT (`the day` `the day the court reads the provision` `is before` `the day it came into operation`))
    AND `the day` `the day the court reads the provision` `is before` `the expiry day`
    WHERE
        `the expiry day` MEANS
            IF `an earlier expiry date is specified` AND (`the day` `the earlier expiry date` `is before` (`the 5th anniversary of` `the day it came into operation`))
            THEN `the earlier expiry date`
            ELSE `the 5th anniversary of` `the day it came into operation`

-- s 32(1) "So far as it is possible to do so consistently with their purpose, all statutory provisions must be
-- interpreted in a way that is compatible with human rights." s 32(3): an incompatible Act stays valid. s 36(5): a
-- declaration of inconsistent interpretation does not affect validity and does not "create in any person any legal
-- right or give rise to any civil cause of action". s 49(1): all Acts, whenever passed. s 49(2) "This Charter does not
-- affect any proceedings commenced or concluded before the commencement of Part 2" (1 January 2007). s 2(2): s 32 in
-- operation from 1 January 2008.
DECLARE `Reading compatibly` IS ONE OF
    `yes: so far as it is possible to do so consistently with its purpose, the provision must be interpreted compatibly with human rights (s 32(1)); if it cannot be, it stays valid (s 32(3)), and a declaration of inconsistent interpretation gives me no right or cause of action (s 36(5))`
    `no: s 32 applies to statutory provisions (Victorian Acts and subordinate instruments, s 3), and this law is not one`
    `no: to the extent of an override declaration in force, the Charter has no application to the provision (s 31(6))`
    `no: the Charter does not affect a proceeding commenced before 1 January 2007 (s 49(2))`
    `no: s 32 was not in operation before 1 January 2008 (s 2(2))`

GIVEN `the law` IS A `Kind of law`
      `the day my proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the court reads the provision` IS A DATE
      `an override declaration was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it came into operation` IS A DATE
      `an earlier expiry date is specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier expiry date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Reading compatibly`
`s 32 -- reading compatibly` `the law` `the day my proceeding was commenced` `the day the court reads the provision` `an override declaration was made` `the day it came into operation` `an earlier expiry date is specified` `the earlier expiry date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 3 -- a statutory provision` `the law`)
        THEN `no: s 32 applies to statutory provisions (Victorian Acts and subordinate instruments, s 3), and this law is not one`
        IF `the day` `the day my proceeding was commenced` `is before` `the day Part 2 came into operation`
        THEN `no: the Charter does not affect a proceeding commenced before 1 January 2007 (s 49(2))`
        IF `the day` `the day the court reads the provision` `is before` `the day Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 came into operation`
        THEN `no: s 32 was not in operation before 1 January 2008 (s 2(2))`
        IF `s 31(6), (7) -- an override declaration is in force` `an override declaration was made` `the day it came into operation` `an earlier expiry date is specified` `the earlier expiry date` `the day the court reads the provision`
        THEN `no: to the extent of an override declaration in force, the Charter has no application to the provision (s 31(6))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: so far as it is possible to do so consistently with its purpose, the provision must be interpreted compatibly with human rights (s 32(1)); if it cannot be, it stays valid (s 32(3)), and a declaration of inconsistent interpretation gives me no right or cause of action (s 36(5))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 35 -- notice to the Attorney-General and the Commission (a duty on me as a party)`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 35(1) "A party to a proceeding must give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General and the Commission
-- if-- (a) in the case of a Supreme Court or County Court proceeding, a question of law arises that relates to the
-- application of this Charter or a question arises with respect to the interpretation of a statutory provision in
-- accordance with this Charter; or (b) in any case, a question is referred to the Supreme Court under section 33."
-- s 35(2) "a notice is not required to be given to-- (a) the Attorney-General if the State is a party ...; or (b) the
-- Commission if the Commission is a party". The prescribed form is in regulations not deposited. The Act sets no time
-- for the notice (fork F8).
DECLARE `Court` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court`
    `the County Court`
    `another court or tribunal (for example the Magistrates' Court or VCAT)`

DECLARE `Notices I must give` IS ONE OF
    `notice in the prescribed form to both the Attorney-General and the Commission (s 35(1))`
    `notice in the prescribed form to the Commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 35(1), (2)(a))`
    `notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General only; none to the Commission, as it is a party (s 35(1), (2)(b))`
    `no notice: both the State and the Commission are parties (s 35(2))`
    `no notice: s 35(1) requires one only for a Charter question in the Supreme Court or the County Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 33`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a Charter question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(1) -- notice is required` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33` IF
        (    ((`the court` EQUALS `the Supreme Court`) OR (`the court` EQUALS `the County Court`))
         AND `a Charter question arises`)
    OR `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33`

GIVEN `the court` IS A `Court`
      `a Charter question arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission is a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notices I must give`
`s 35 -- notices I must give` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33` `the State is a party` `the Commission is a party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 35(1) -- notice is required` `the court` `a Charter question arises` `a question was referred to the Supreme Court under s 33`)
        THEN `no notice: s 35(1) requires one only for a Charter question in the Supreme Court or the County Court, or a question referred to the Supreme Court under s 33`
        IF `the State is a party` AND `the Commission is a party`
        THEN `no notice: both the State and the Commission are parties (s 35(2))`
        IF `the State is a party`
        THEN `notice in the prescribed form to the Commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 35(1), (2)(a))`
        IF `the Commission is a party`
        THEN `notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General only; none to the Commission, as it is a party (s 35(1), (2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `notice in the prescribed form to both the Attorney-General and the Commission (s 35(1))`

-- The regulative rule. s 35(1) as a duty on me: I MUST give each notice the section requires (RAND where both are
-- required). No WITHIN: the Act fixes no time, so the duty waits until done (fork F8); there is no LEST in the Act.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `I`
DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF
    `give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General`
    `give notice in the prescribed form to the Commission`

GIVEN `the notices` IS A `Notices I must give`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 35(1) -- my duty to notify` `the notices` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the notices`
    WHEN `notice in the prescribed form to both the Attorney-General and the Commission (s 35(1))` THEN
        (PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General`)
        RAND
        (PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the prescribed form to the Commission`)
    WHEN `notice in the prescribed form to the Commission only; none to the Attorney-General, as the State is a party (s 35(1), (2)(a))` THEN
        PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the prescribed form to the Commission`
    WHEN `notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General only; none to the Commission, as it is a party (s 35(1), (2)(b))` THEN
        PARTY `I` MUST `give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General`
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- Runs the duty over what I have done. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED only; a duty still
-- waiting is a residual, so not FULFILLED. Takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `I gave the Attorney-General notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I gave the Commission notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty is met under` `the rule` `I gave the Attorney-General notice` `I gave the Commission notice` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (IF `I gave the Attorney-General notice` AND `I gave the Commission notice`
                                     THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General` 1), (EVENT `I` `give notice in the prescribed form to the Commission` 1)
                                     ELSE IF `I gave the Attorney-General notice`
                                          THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the prescribed form to the Attorney-General` 1)
                                          ELSE IF `I gave the Commission notice`
                                               THEN LIST (EVENT `I` `give notice in the prescribed form to the Commission` 1)
                                               ELSE LIST (WAITUNTIL 1))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Notices given` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have given every notice s 35 requires`
    `yes: s 35 requires no notice from me`
    `no: I have still to give a notice s 35 requires`
